# MIDAS (MASTER-based Impact Flux and Damage Assessment Software) Surface Definition File
# [v3.0.0, 11/2018]
#
#===============================================================================
#
# 1) Analysis Settings
#
#--------------------------------------:----------------------------------------
# Target type                                                                   
  1               -(1:3)-            1 = sphere
#                                    2 = randomly tumbling plate                 
#                                    3 = oriented surface (defined in .sdf file) 
#
#===============================================================================
#
# 2) Surface Definitions
#
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 
# Surface orientation (1,2,3) and offset angles A and h: 
#               - 1 = earth oriented
#                     -180deg<A<180deg :  azimuth of surface normal
#                      -90deg<h<90deg  :  elevation of surface normal
#               - 2 = sun oriented
#                     -180deg<A<180deg :  right asc. deviation from sun LOS
#                      -90deg<h<90deg  :  declination deviation from sun LOS
#               - 3 = inertially fixed
#                     -180deg<A<180deg :  right asc. of surface normal
#                      -90deg<h<90deg  :  declination of surface normal
#
# Surface area: - required for computing the number of impacts [m^2]
#
# Ballistic limit equation (BLE) type (1,9) :
#               - Single Wall Equation 
#                   1 = Cour-Palais thin plate
#                   2 = Cour-Palais galss target
#                   3 = User-defined BLE parameters
#               - Multiple Wall Equation 
#                   4 = (Whipple Shield - Christansen)
#                   5 = Multiple Wall Equation (ESA tripple wall)
#                   6 = User-defined BLE parameters
#               - Schaefer-Ryan-Lambert (SRL) Equation 
#                   7 = SRL Original
#                   8 = SRL Rudolph recalibration
#                   9 = User-defined BLE parameters
#
# Number of user defined set of BLE parameters (1,10) :
#               - considered for BLE type 3, 6 & 9
#
# Wall thickness (mm) / density (g/cm^3) :
#               - considered for BLE type 1 - 3
#                
# Spacing between wall and shield (cm):
#               - considered for BLE type 4 - 6
#
# Shield (outer bumper) thickness (cm) / density (g/cm^3):
#               - considered for BLE type 4 - 9
#
# Inner bumper thickness (cm):
#               - considered for BLE type 7 - 9
#
# Equivalent MLI/CFRP/cable thickness (cm):
#               - considered for BLE type 7 - 9
#
# Spacing between wall and inner bumper (cm):
#               - considered for BLE type 7 - 9
#
# Spacing between inner and outer bumpers (cm):
#               - considered for BLE type 7 - 9
#
# Yield stress of cover plate (ksi):
#               - considered for BLE type 7 - 9
#
# Descripton of the surface (CHAR*30)
#
#----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On/Off  Orien-  Angle A  Angle h  Area   BLE  BLE  Wall      Wall     Spacing Shield/OB  Shield   Inner Bump   Equiv MLI  Bumpers  Inner to  Wall   Description
# Switch  tation                           type No.  thickness density  between thickness  density  thickness    thickness  spacing  wall spc  yield
